{
  "title": "Ingredient parser: a mixed-number package size without parens (\"1 14 1/2-ounce can\") ends up in the item",
  "description": "\"1 14 1/2-ounce can diced tomatoes\" (smittenkitchen red bean chili) parses as {amount: 1, unit: null} with item \"14 1/2-ounce can diced tomatoes\", and \"2 15 1/2-ounce cans kidney beans\" is the same. \
The single-number form \"1 15-ounce can\" already reads as one \"15-ounce can\" in the measurement grammar (measure.rs hyphenated_unit), but there a count followed by a mixed number reads \"1 14 1/2\" as the amount, or stops before the size. \
The parenthesized form (\"1 (14 1/2-ounce) can\") now puts \"14 1/2-ounce\" in the note for quantity.rs to join with \"can\", so the unparenthesized form should read as {1, \"14 1/2-ounce can\"} or the same note shape. \
Rerun make pipeline; expect a few data/ diffs.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "bug",
